"L" <L_1_L_0@yahoo.com> wrote:
>I consider each symbol class to indicate monsters with common
>biological traits (hence blessed _geno_cide.) I dislike placing
>monsters of the same species in different classes, (which is why I want
>to move rust monsters to 'a' and disenchanters to 'q', except that I
>don't know what to put in the now-vacant 'R' class)

'a'?  Y'what?  Rust monsters are not described as insects in Nethack,
and the original source material depicts them as having a definitely
non-insectoid form.  The creature depicted on page 83 of the first
edition Monster Manual has four clearly endoskeletal legs (complete with
long spindly toes!), simple eyes (you can see the pupils), and a clearly
vertebrate tail.

It does not have a tripartite body structure of head, thorax, and
abdomen; it does not have compound eyes; it does not have an
exoskeleton; it does not have six legs.  It is not by any reasonable
stretch of the imagination an insect.

'R' should contain one monster, if you're moving disenchanters to 'q'.
It should contain rust monsters.
